# ============================================================================
# S163 — this file used to live at `docker/.dockerignore`.
#
# Docker reads `.dockerignore` ONLY from the build CONTEXT ROOT, and every build
# (docker-compose.yml, .github/workflows/docker.yml, docker/README.md) uses
# `context: .` — so at `docker/.dockerignore` it was INERT. Two consequences,
# both live:
#
#   * `COPY . /var/www/html/` runs AFTER `composer install --no-dev`, so the
#     host's dev `vendor/` (phpunit, mockery, …) was copied straight over the
#     pruned one — `--no-dev` bought nothing on a local build;
#   * `.logs/` shipped INSIDE the image. On this checkout that is ~175 MB of
#     application logs containing `api_key` / `token` / `password` strings.
#
# Moving the file is the fix. The original body is preserved verbatim below;
# the only additions are at the end, and they exist because Docker's patterns
# are matched per path — a bare `*.log` / `node_modules/` matches the CONTEXT
# ROOT ONLY, so it never excluded `.logs/app-*.log` or `web-ui/node_modules/`.
# ============================================================================
.git
.gitignore
.coverage
.phpunit.cache
coverage/
coverage-report/
vendor/
node_modules/
*.md
docker-compose*.yml
.dockerignore
Dockerfile*
.env*
phpstan*.neon*
phpunit.xml*
.git/
tests/
docs/
plans/
*.log
.phpunit.result.cache

# --- S163 additions: the patterns above only match the context ROOT ---------
# `.logs/` is the application log directory (config/logger.php). It is the
# reason this file's placement mattered: it carries `api_key`/`token`/`password`
# strings and was being baked into the published image.
.logs/
**/*.log
**/node_modules/
coverage.xml
.phpunit-assertion-escapes.json
